      "problem": "What is the solution to $z-1\\ge -4?$",
      "worked_solution": "To isolate $z,$ we need to perform the *opposite* of *subtracting* $1,$ which is *adding* $1.$\nRemember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & \\ge -4 \\\\ z-1+1 & \\ge -4+1 \\\\ z+0 & \\ge -3 \\\\ z & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z\\ge -3.$",
